Subject: Record a summary in error recovery for a version that has none

Record a summary for a version in the error state that has none.

The copy of the runtime of the tree-sitter-cpp fork has this repair. The fork commit is
eca35f6.

Error recovery goes back to a state of the summary that the parser
records when it detects an error. A version in the error state can have
no summary. A merge keeps the summary of one version only, and a
reduction of a non-terminal extra makes a new version. A directive in
the error state is such an extra. Without a summary, the version skips
each token until the end of the file, and the root node is ERROR.

ts_parser__recover now records the summary of the stack below the ERROR
at the top of the stack when the version has none.

On the corpus at 7cf7762, the root node is ERROR in 38 files before and
20 files after. 20 files change, and no file without an error changes.

The repair is not specific to a language. A version in the error state with no summary skips each
token until the end of the input.

Risk for upstream: low.

The patch applies to the upstream tag v0.27.0, after the patches with a smaller number. The
series compiles with `-Wall -Wextra` and no warning.

The comments hold the marker "(tree-sitter-cpp fork)". Remove the marker before you send the
patch upstream.

diff -ruN a/lib/src/parser.c b/lib/src/parser.c
--- a/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-15 19:00:45.682701039 +0200
+++ b/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-15 19:00:45.697706219 +0200
@@ -1300,6 +1300,16 @@
   unsigned node_count_since_error = ts_stack_node_count_since_error(self->stack, version);
   unsigned current_error_cost = ts_stack_error_cost(self->stack, version);
 
+  // A version in the error state can have no summary. A merge keeps the summary of one version
+  // only. A reduction of a non-terminal extra, for example a directive, makes a new version with
+  // no summary. Without a summary, the version skips each token until the end of the file. Record
+  // the summary of the stack below the ERROR at the top. The depths then agree with the summary
+  // of ts_parser__handle_error (tree-sitter-cpp fork).
+  if (!summary) {
+    ts_stack_record_summary(self->stack, version, MAX_SUMMARY_DEPTH, node_count_since_error > 0 ? 1 : 0);
+    summary = ts_stack_get_summary(self->stack, version);
+  }
+
   // When the parser is in the error state, there are two strategies for recovering with a
   // given lookahead token:
   // 1. Find a previous state on the stack in which that lookahead token would be valid. Then,
@@ -1559,7 +1569,7 @@
     ts_assert(did_merge);
   }
 
-  ts_stack_record_summary(self->stack, version, MAX_SUMMARY_DEPTH);
+  ts_stack_record_summary(self->stack, version, MAX_SUMMARY_DEPTH, 0);
 
   // Begin recovery with the current lookahead node, rather than waiting for the
   // next turn of the parse loop. This ensures that the tree accounts for the
diff -ruN a/lib/src/stack.c b/lib/src/stack.c
--- a/lib/src/stack.c	2026-08-30 18:49:12.000000000 +0200
+++ b/lib/src/stack.c	2026-09-15 19:00:45.697209603 +0200
@@ -601,12 +601,14 @@
 typedef struct {
   StackSummary *summary;
   unsigned max_depth;
+  unsigned skipped_depth;
 } SummarizeStackSession;
 
 forceinline StackAction summarize_stack_callback(void *payload, const StackIterator *iterator) {
   SummarizeStackSession *session = payload;
   TSStateId state = iterator->node->state;
-  unsigned depth = iterator->subtree_count;
+  if (iterator->subtree_count < session->skipped_depth) return StackActionNone;
+  unsigned depth = iterator->subtree_count - session->skipped_depth;
   if (depth > session->max_depth) return StackActionStop;
   for (unsigned i = session->summary->size - 1; i + 1 > 0; i--) {
     StackSummaryEntry entry = *array_get(session->summary, i);
@@ -621,10 +623,11 @@
   return StackActionNone;
 }
 
-void ts_stack_record_summary(Stack *self, StackVersion version, unsigned max_depth) {
+void ts_stack_record_summary(Stack *self, StackVersion version, unsigned max_depth, unsigned skipped_depth) {
   SummarizeStackSession session = {
     .summary = ts_malloc(sizeof(StackSummary)),
-    .max_depth = max_depth
+    .max_depth = max_depth,
+    .skipped_depth = skipped_depth,
   };
   array_init(session.summary);
   stack__iter(self, version, summarize_stack_callback, &session, -1);
diff -ruN a/lib/src/stack.h b/lib/src/stack.h
--- a/lib/src/stack.h	2026-08-30 18:49:12.000000000 +0200
+++ b/lib/src/stack.h	2026-09-15 19:00:45.697270127 +0200
@@ -85,7 +85,10 @@
 
